      "reasoning": "All four earlier answers are confirmed by their own captured worked solutions. q-103836: cotangent is undefined at x=n\\pi, has period \\pi, and is defined at \\pi/2; the proposed asymptote set includes \\pi/2, and the proposed domain is incorrect. Thus only III is true. q-70669: cotangent is unbounded below, is undefined at -4\\pi, and equals zero at -3\\pi/2. Thus I and III are true. The stray $$ tokens are source formatting errors and do not change the mathematics. q-36011: each restricted linear branch in I and II is strictly monotone, whereas III includes branches with overlapping output values and fails the horizontal line test. q-66679: the parabola is strictly decreasing on I and strictly increasing on II; III contains 0 and 2, with f(0)=f(2)=-1, so it is not injective. No captured grade is provided; each confirmation uses the owning question's worked solution.",
