    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-103840",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d02418c3-4c04-57b8-8f10-18858b1759ab",
      "knowledge_point": "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Cotangent Function",
      "problem": "If $cot⁡x=\\sqrt{2}$ for some $x,$ then find the value of $cot⁡(x-9\\pi ).$",
      "worked_solution": "The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡x=cot⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡x & =cot⁡(x+(-9)\\cdot \\pi ) \\\\  & =cot⁡(x-9\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cot⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ then $cot⁡(x-9\\pi )=\\sqrt{2}.$",
      "answer_fields": [
